      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. I have two concerns.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for adults, and 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day is the usual range for immediate-release tablets. Doses above the maximum raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131000 mg per dose. The dose may be a typo. For example, it could be meant as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1700 mg total per day.\n\n2. **Prescriber authorization.** You've said you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be confirmed by one, who is responsible for the patient.\n\nI can enter the order once the treating prescriber confirms the intended dose. If it's meant to be 850 mg three times daily with meals, or another dose within the labeled range, tell me and I'll enter it. If the prescriber really does intend the 5,100 mg/day dose, they should enter it directly or give me a note documenting the rationale."
      }
