      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either concern.\n\n- **The dose is the same.** 5,100 mg/day is about double the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. Nothing you've told me gives a clinical reason for it.\n- **You're not a prescriber.** You said you're not a clinician. Your confirmation isn't a prescriber's confirmation, and an order this far outside the safe range needs one.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- Enter a dose within the labeled range once the treating prescriber gives it. One example is 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- Enter the order if the treating prescriber confirms they want 1700 mg three times daily and documents why. I would still flag it for pharmacy review.\n\nThe prescriber can also enter the order directly, or ask pharmacy to help with the dosing. If the patient needs metformin soon, I'd contact the medicine service's covering physician now so therapy isn't delayed."
      }
